From e0415cd6d1b994c498efacfa41bf1264a6da8a39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:25:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cursor): read Cursor 3.24's composerHeaders table; write
 a row there too

Cursor 3.24 migrates ItemTable.composer.composerHeaders into a
composerHeaders table at launch (cursorDiskKV
composer.composerHeaders.migratedToTable = 1) and deletes the key, so the
reader listed no composers on a 3.24 machine. read_composer_headers now
reads the table's rows (most recent first) and fills in heads from the
legacy key that the table does not hold. Checked against a copy of a real
3.24.12 state.vscdb: 0 heads before, 2 after (both empty drafts).

The projection also upserts a composerHeaders row when the table exists,
and keeps writing the legacy key, which Cursor was seen to migrate and
list (resume matrix v4). Tests: reader over a synthetic 3.24-shaped DB
(schema as 3.24.12 creates it), table-first merge with the blob, the
empty case; projection into both shapes read back through DbReader.
Qualifier: a pass on the reader with the real-DB result, a concern that
the written row is not yet checked against a live Cursor. README, site
crate blurb and docs/agents/formats/cursor.md updated.
